  "verbalization": "Glabratolide appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step mechanism involving the modulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like (LSD4D-like), which is a key enzyme in the demethylation of lysine residues on histones and other proteins. This enzyme is targeted by 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Interiorin, both of which are implicated in the regulation of gene expression and cellular processes. The final pathway links Glabratolide to RWLeu4 through a series of targets, suggesting that it may influence cellular functions by modulating the activity of these enzymes. The evidence suggests that Glabratolide could act as a modulator of the downstream effects of these targets, potentially affecting gene expression and cellular behavior. The integration of multiple targets and the presence of a consistent pathway from Glabratolide to RWLeu4 indicate a plausible mechanistic link, though further validation with direct experimental evidence would be necessary to confirm the exact role of Glabratolide in the regulation of RWLeu4.",
